+## AP-09 local preparation storage · 2026-11-26
+
+`RouteAmendmentDraft.Persistence` captures geometry, stable plotted/anchor IDs,
+partial entries and accepted legacy values, mode/provenance, editor/inspection
+context and full Undo history. It excludes workspace visibility, plotting,
+transient gesture/delete offers and map choices. Recovery validates Flight and
+route-anchor identities before projection, preserves stale-departure work and
+normalizes interaction from geometry. `CockpitFeatureState.restoreAmendmentDraft`
+installs it hidden and cannot replace pending/activated operational amendments.
+
+`AmendmentDraftStore` accepts a schema-versioned Flight-keyed envelope with revision,
+recording sequence and snapshot payload. `DiskAmendmentDraftStore` owns atomic local
+JSON replacement in a sibling `FlightPlans-amendment-drafts` directory, outside
+recording packages. It rejects older revisions and preserves unsupported,
+mismatched or corrupt envelopes. `InMemoryAmendmentDraftStore` supplies injected
+failure/retry tests. Codable additions to immutable navigation/value types support
+this local snapshot only; operational DTOs and schemas are unchanged.
+
+`AmendmentDraftPersistence` owns a single serialized, coalescing writer independent
+of view-task cancellation. Status publication checks revision identity; failures
+retain the latest memory snapshot. Delete waits for in-flight writes, prevents
+competing edits and reports success only after removal. An unreadable recovered
+snapshot quarantines that Flight's draft writes for the process lifetime. It does
+not block ordinary navigation or remove the saved bytes.
+
+`RootView` owns/injects the store/coordinator, observes durable draft state and
+attempts a final save on scene departure. Flight recovery completes through its
+existing coordinator before a matching unarmed draft is attached. The recovered
+Flight exposes the greatest existing amendment-event sequence as a read-only
+fence: a draft saved before a later operational amendment is obsolete, including
+when cleanup failed and pending cancellation subsequently committed. No new
+operational event is generated by draft persistence. Arm cleanup runs only after
+the existing durable transaction succeeds. AP-11/AP-12's future operational
+redesign remains outside this checkpoint.
+
+`RouteAmendmentConsole` places native F10 retry content within its existing scroll
+extent; `CockpitView` reuses the independent F07 unsaved badge and native discard
+confirmation. DEBUG C extends the shared disposable bootstrap with a selected
+heading-only leg, nil duration and cues. Failure switches affect only injected
+draft operations. See the [AP-09 matrix/ledger](../reconciliations/2026-11-23-route-amendment-preparation/evidence/ap-09-implementation.md)
+for evidence, remaining checks and separate owner acceptance.
+
